# Copy this file to .env ONLY if you need to override the API host.
#
# You usually do NOT need a .env. src/constants/api.js derives the backend
# host from Expo's hostUri, so scanning the QR on a physical device already
# points at the right machine, and it keeps working when your LAN IP changes.
#
# Expo only inlines variables prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ — a plain API_BASE_URL
# is silently ignored.
#
# Override examples:
#   Android Emulator: http://10.0.2.2:3000/api
#   iOS Simulator:    http://localhost:3000/api
#   Physical device:  http://<your-local-ip>:3000/api
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000/api
